ce": "discovery", "step_id": "ref-13", "summary": "The change log shows DE search ranking is owned by the server-side search-ranker. Relevance, a ranking-side signal, fell the same way as CTR and conversion."}], "explained_share": 1.0, "first_change_ts": "2026-11-27T03:00:00Z", "id": "H1", "root_node": "search_relevance", "segment": {"country": "DE"}, "statement": "search-ranker v7.2 (DE-scoped, 2026-11-27T03:00Z) halved DE search_relevance, which halved search_ctr and search_conversion across all platforms.", "status": "supported"}, "suggested_actions": ["Roll back search-ranker v7.2 in DE to the previous version and check that DE search_relevance and search_conversion return to about 0.875 and 0.125.", "Diff the v7.2 ranking model and features against v7.1 and add a relevance guardrail to the ranker rollout.", "Restore the client_errors and trace data feeds so client-side faults can be ruled out in future incidents."], "summary": "DE search_conversion fell to 0.0625 from an expected 0.125 (delta -0.0625, -50%) in 2026-11-27 03:00\u201305:00Z. The data is fresh (completeness 1.0). The drop affects only DE electronics and is the same on android, iOS and web (each -0.0625). FR, the control, did not move. Upstream, DE search_relevance halved (0.875\u21920.4375) and search_ctr halved (0.5\u21920.25), and all three metrics first changed at 03:00Z. That is the same hour the unplanned, DE-scoped search-ranker v7.2 release shipped. Two other releases are ruled out. The Android app release at 01:00 came two hours before the drop, and the drop is not specific to Android. The search-ui v3.0 release was scoped to FR, and FR stayed flat. The Skeptic found nothing that makes this innocent: there was no planned event, and seasonality does not explain it (spread 0, z=-25).", "verdict": "CONFIRMED"}, "name": "submit", "toolset_name": null, "type": "tool_use"}], "context_management": null, "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011ChGH51WN2XgPg75Ryw9dy", "input_transformations": null, "mod